  const response = await fetch(url, { method });
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);
  return response.json();
}
await request(`${a}/write`, 'POST');
console.log(await request(`${b}/value`));
await request(`${b}/value`, 'DELETE');
console.log(await request(`${a}/value`));
await request(`${a}/write`, 'POST');
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1100));
console.log(await request(`${b}/value`));
```

Expected client values are {hit:true,value:false}, then {hit:false}, then {hit:false}. They are unobserved expectations. The exact remote constructor, deletion behavior, miss carrier, and timeout behavior were not retained in primary-source captures. A miss may be null or undefined in the candidate stack; only those values mean absence.

For restart, rewrite the key, restart Redis without persistence, then GET http://127.0.0.1:3002/value. For outage, stop Redis before that GET. Record whether the stack throws, hangs, or returns absence. No retained source establishes its outage answer; an absence answer would fail Jet’s transport-error requirement.

## Evidence boundary

The retained Nest page documents in-memory defaults, cache injection, get, set, and milliseconds for expiry. It names Redis but does not retain a complete remote constructor or exact remote package pin. Complete peer code above is authored composition. Do not relabel it as captured or executed support.

